Feature: Calculate New Enrollment Review TAT and generate tat_report table

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog database "purgo_databricks" and schema "purgo_playground"
    And source tables "pat_case" and "sr_activity" exist in the schema
    And "pat_case" contains columns: case_id, service_request_type, sr_created_date, <other_pat_case_columns>
    And "sr_activity" contains columns: case_id, subject, status, last_modified_date, <other_sr_activity_columns>
    And output table "tat_report" will be created in "purgo_playground" schema

  Scenario Outline: Calculate total_time_elapsed for New Enrollment Review TAT
    Given a "pat_case" record with case_id = <case_id>, service_request_type = <service_request_type>, sr_created_date = <sr_created_date>
    And related "sr_activity" records for case_id = <case_id> with subject = <subject>, status = <status>, last_modified_date = <last_modified_date_list>
    When the PySpark script processes the data
    Then if service_request_type != "Patient Foundation", the record is excluded from tat_report
    And if no matching "sr_activity" record with subject = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" and status = "Completed" exists for the case_id, total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And if sr_created_date is NULL, total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And if minimum last_modified_date is NULL, total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And if minimum last_modified_date < sr_created_date, total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And if minimum last_modified_date = sr_created_date, total_time_elapsed is 0
    And if minimum last_modified_date > sr_created_date, total_time_elapsed is the count of business days (excluding weekends) between sr_created_date and minimum last_modified_date (date only)
    And tat_report contains all columns from "pat_case" plus total_time_elapsed as integer (nullable)
    And tat_report is written to "purgo_playground.tat_report" (overwrite mode)

    Examples:
      | case_id | service_request_type | sr_created_date | subject                              | status      | last_modified_date_list           | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 1001    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-05,2024-06-07]           | 4                          |
      | 1002    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-01]                      | 0                          |
      | 1003    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-05-30]                      | NULL                       |
      | 1004    | Patient Foundation  | NULL            | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-05]                      | NULL                       |
      | 1005    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [NULL]                            | NULL                       |
      | 1006    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Other Activity                       | Completed   | [2024-06-05]                      | NULL                       |
      | 1007    | Other Service       | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-05]                      | Excluded                   |
      | 1008    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-08,2024-06-09]           | 5                          |
      | 1009    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | [2024-06-02,2024-06-03]           | 1                          |
      | 1010    | Patient Foundation  | 2024-06-01      | Perform New Enrollment Review Activity| Completed   | []                                 | NULL                       |

  Scenario: Validate business day calculation for total_time_elapsed
    Given sr_created_date = 2024-06-01 (Saturday)
    And minimum last_modified_date = 2024-06-07 (Friday)
    When calculating total_time_elapsed
    Then only business days (Monday-Friday) between 2024-06-01 and 2024-06-07 are counted
    And weekends (2024-06-01, 2024-06-02, 2024-06-08, 2024-06-09) are excluded
    And total_time_elapsed = 5

  Scenario: Validate NULL handling for missing dates
    Given sr_created_date is NULL
    Or minimum last_modified_date is NULL
    When calculating total_time_elapsed
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL

  Scenario: Validate exclusion of non-matching service_request_type
    Given a "pat_case" record with service_request_type != "Patient Foundation"
    When processing for tat_report
    Then the record is excluded from tat_report

  Scenario: Validate exclusion of non-matching sr_activity subject/status
    Given a "pat_case" record with service_request_type = "Patient Foundation"
    And no "sr_activity" record with subject = "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" and status = "Completed" for the case_id
    When processing for tat_report
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL

  Scenario: Validate output schema
    Given tat_report is generated
    Then tat_report contains all columns from "pat_case"
    And tat_report contains total_time_elapsed column as integer (nullable)

  Scenario: Validate overwrite mode for tat_report
    Given tat_report table already exists in "purgo_playground" schema
    When the PySpark script runs
    Then tat_report is overwritten with new results

  Scenario Outline: Validate data type and value constraints for total_time_elapsed
    Given calculated total_time_elapsed = <value>
    When writing to tat_report
    Then total_time_elapsed is integer if not NULL
    And total_time_elapsed is NULL if invalid or missing

    Examples:
      | value |
      | 0     |
      | 1     |
      | 5     |
      | NULL  |

  Scenario: Validate duplicate case_id handling
    Given multiple "pat_case" records with the same case_id
    When processing for tat_report
    Then each record is processed independently based on its sr_created_date and matching sr_activity records

  Scenario: Validate type mismatches in input data
    Given sr_created_date or last_modified_date is not a valid date
    When processing for tat_report
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And an error is logged for invalid date format

# END
